as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nFor stability, we require that the following condition holds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(\\lambda Δx)| & <1 \\\\ |1-\\lambda Δx| & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this gives\n\n$$\n0<\\lambda Δx<2.\n$$\n\nThis means that Euler's method is stable when applied to the test equation for values in the region $0<\\lambda Δx<2.$ Of the given values:\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.5,$ falls *within* the given region,\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.8,$ falls *within* the given region,\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=2.1,$ falls *outside* the given region.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=3,$ falls *outside* the given region.\n\nHence, Euler's method is **unstable** for the values $\\lambda Δx=2.1,$ and $\\lambda Δx=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III and IV only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186372673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372671 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d82b587d-88f5-5209-8711-b68207cf6390" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372672 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372672 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372672 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "caa6f4b3-cc01-5d85-9a4d-de489c723ea6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372673 #edb/ref 1080 "III and IV only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372673 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372673 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fab3b6cc-ea3a-5b82-